<p>
  A team is the paid plan with more than one person in it. Everybody in your
  account occupies a seat, and a seat is
  $<%= StripeBilling::PRICE_PER_SEAT_USD %> per user per month. The free plan
  has exactly <%= Quotas::Limits::FREE_SEATS %>.
</p>

<h2>Inviting somebody</h2>

<ol>
  <li>Go to <strong>Settings &rarr; Users</strong> and enter the person's email address.</li>
  <li>If your subscription is already paying for a spare seat, the invitation goes out straight away and nothing is charged.</li>
  <li>If every seat is taken, we show you what your card will be charged <em>today</em> for the rest of the current billing period, and what the subscription will cost from the next renewal. Nothing happens until you confirm.</li>
  <li>Once the payment goes through, the invitation is sent. The person chooses their own name and password when they accept.</li>
</ol>

<p>
  An invitation lasts <%= BillingLifecycle::INVITE_TOKEN_DAYS %> days and holds
  the seat while it waits. Pending invitations are listed on Settings &rarr;
  Users with their expiry date, and can be resent or cancelled.
</p>

<aside class="help-callout">
  <p>
    <strong>Good to know:</strong> you always see the exact amount before a
    seat is bought. That figure is a preview &mdash; asking for it creates
    nothing and charges nothing &mdash; and the moment it was priced from is
    the moment the real charge uses, so the invoice you get is the one you
    agreed to.
  </p>
</aside>

<h2>If the person already has their own account</h2>

<p>
  That is not an error. The invitation page says so and offers to
  <strong>join this team</strong>: accepting moves them across, bringing their
  templates, folders and documents with them, and their old account is
  archived rather than deleted. Documents that account has already signed stay
  verifiable exactly as they are.
</p>

<p>
  Because it is a move between two organisations, the keys their old account
  issued stop working &mdash; API tokens, "remember me", and every browser they
  were signed in on except the one they accepted from. We tell them all of this
  before they press the button. The move is refused, with a plain explanation
  of what to settle first, if their old account still has other people in it,
  still has a paid subscription, is frozen for an unpaid card, or is scheduled
  for deletion.
</p>

<h2>Removing people, and seats going back down</h2>

<p>
  A seat comes back when you remove someone, make them read-only, or when an
  invitation lapses or is cancelled. The subscription then bills for fewer
  seats from your next renewal. Additions are charged immediately; reductions
  are not credited or refunded mid-cycle &mdash; the next invoice is simply
  smaller. An account can never lose its last administrator, so removing or
  demoting the only admin is refused.
</p>

<h2>Dropping back to the free plan with a team</h2>

<p>
  Nobody is deleted. The administrator who signed in most recently keeps full
  access and everybody else becomes read-only: they can still sign in, read,
  download and export, but not create or change anything. Settings &rarr; Users
  has <strong>Give full access</strong> and <strong>Make read-only</strong> on
  each person, so you decide who holds the seats.
</p>

